\title{zucrypt: Cryptography Without System Dependencies}
\description{
Cryptographic functions over raw vectors, including message digests, keyed-hash message authentication codes (HMAC), Advanced Encryption Standard (AES) encryption, constant-time comparison and secure erasure, backed by a bundled and pinned copy of the 'Mbed TLS' project's cryptography library, 'TF-PSA-Crypto' (\url{https://github.com/Mbed-TLS/TF-PSA-Crypto}). No system cryptographic library, 'Java' or 'Python' is required at install or run time. The function set follows the 'openssl' package's, so that code written against it can move over by changing a prefix. Algorithm names are matched exactly, and failures are reported as structured conditions. The same primitives are published to other packages as a static archive and as a registered C interface, so that a package can call them from C without going through R.
}
